{"task_id": "Mbpp/2", "solution": "def similar_elements(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute and return an iterable of elements present in both sequences a and b.\n\n    Parameters:\n    - a: first sequence (list/tuple or other sequence-like iterable)\n    - b: second sequence (list/tuple or other sequence-like iterable)\n\n    Returns:\n    - An iterable over elements appearing in both inputs (element equality used for membership checks).\n    \"\"\"\n    b_set = set(b)\n    yielded_elements = set()\n    for item_a in a:\n        if item_a in b_set and item_a not in yielded_elements:\n            yield item_a\n            yielded_elements.add(item_a)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/7", "solution": "from typing import List\nclass TextProcessor:\n    def find_char_long(self, input: str) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Tokenizes the input string and filters words by minimum length.\"\"\"\n        tokens = self.tokenize(input)\n        return self.filterByLength(tokens, minLen=4)\n\n    def tokenize(self, input: str) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Splits the input string into words using whitespace.\"\"\"\n        return input.split()\n\n    def filterByLength(self, tokens: List[str], minLen: int = 4) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Filters a list of tokens, keeping only those meeting the minimum length.\"\"\"\n        return [t for t in tokens if len(t) >= minLen]\ndef find_char_long(input: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all words in a string that are at least 4 characters long.\n    Tokenizes by whitespace and preserves original casing.\n    \"\"\"\n    tp = TextProcessor()\n    return tp.find_char_long(input)"}
