{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "def Find_Min(sublists: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the sublist from 'sublists' that has the minimum length.\n    Raises ValueError if input is empty or TypeError if elements are not lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not sublists:\n        raise ValueError(\"sublists must be non-empty\")\n\n    for sublist_item in sublists:\n        if not isinstance(sublist_item, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"all elements of sublists must be lists\")\n\n    min_sublist = sublists[0]\n    min_length = len(min_sublist)\n\n    for i in range(1, len(sublists)):\n        current_sublist = sublists[i]\n        current_length = len(current_sublist)\n\n        if current_length < min_length:\n            min_length = current_length\n            min_sublist = current_sublist\n\n    return min_sublist"}
