{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(sorted_list: list, target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position (index) of an element in a sorted list.\n    If the target is not found, returns -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(sorted_list) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if sorted_list[mid] == target:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Look for a later occurrence in the right half\n        elif sorted_list[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # sorted_list[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
