{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Natural numbers are integers greater than or equal to 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Normalize the lower bound to be at least 1.\n    effective_l = max(l, 1)\n\n    # If the effective lower bound is greater than the upper bound, the range contains no numbers.\n    if effective_l > r:\n        return 0\n\n    # Determine the first odd number in the normalized range.\n    first_odd = effective_l\n    if first_odd % 2 == 0:\n        first_odd += 1\n\n    # If the first odd number is now out of the range, there are no odd numbers.\n    if first_odd > r:\n        return 0\n\n    # Determine the last odd number in the normalized range.\n    last_odd = r\n    if last_odd % 2 == 0:\n        last_odd -= 1\n\n    # If the last odd number is now less than the first odd, there are no odd numbers.\n    if last_odd < first_odd:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate the number of terms (odd numbers) using the arithmetic progression formula.\n    # The common difference is 2.\n    num_terms = (last_odd - first_odd) // 2 + 1\n\n    # Calculate the sum using the arithmetic progression sum formula: S_n = n/2 * (a_1 + a_n).\n    total_sum = num_terms * (first_odd + last_odd) // 2\n\n    return total_sum"}
