{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "def check_smaller(first, second) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if each element of second tuple is smaller than its corresponding element in the first tuple.\n    Raises:\n      TypeError: if either argument is not a tuple\n      ValueError: if tuple lengths differ\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(first, tuple) or not isinstance(second, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both first and second must be tuples\")\n    if len(first) != len(second):\n        raise ValueError(\"Tuples must have the same length\")\n    for a, b in zip(first, second):\n        if not (b < a):\n            return False\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/632", "solution": "def move_zero(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Reorder input_list elements so non-zero elements (element != 0) appear first in original order,\n    followed by zeros (element == 0). Raise TypeError if input_list is not a list.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"input must be a list\")\n\n    non_zeros = []\n    zeros = []\n    for element in input_list:\n        if element == 0:\n            zeros.append(element)\n        else:\n            non_zeros.append(element)\n    return non_zeros + zeros"}
